WEBVTT

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.847
What do you think
you're doing, Doc?

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.860
An impromptu auditory exam.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:28.861
Did l pass?

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:29.884
With flying colors,

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.726
which leads me to believe
that you did hear me

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.630
when l requested
you meet me this morning.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.235
You're right.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.497
L forgot.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.559
L see.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.505
L realize your Sick Bay
training is purely voluntary,

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.873
but you haven't spent
any time there

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.879
in several weeks, and when I...

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.313
try to find you, you're
always in the holodeck.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.681
Correct me if l'm wrong, Doc,
but we haven't been treating

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.050
anything more serious
than an ingrown toenail.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.145
That's beside the point.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:58.089
If an emergency were to happen,
you must be prepared.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.785
You're too far behind
in your medical texts

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.453
to be wasting your time
in the holodeck!

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.626
Lf it's any consolation,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.427
l have spent most
of the morning immersed

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.457
in a complicated
surgical procedure.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.694
Really?

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.762
A classic case
of atrophied shocks.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.468
They needed to be extracted
to prevent chrome abrasion.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:19.842
It was touch and go for a while,
but the prognosis is excellent.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.972
You'll be ready
for neurosurgery in no time.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:25.178
Take a look at this, Doc.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:30.019
This is a fully stock
1969 Chevy Camaro...

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.183
one of the earliest
muscle cars ever made.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:36.821
Imagine: Northern California,
late 20th century.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.058
You're cruising up Highway 1.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.327
The woofers are pounding.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.834
The wind is whipping
through your hair.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.073
Medieval safety constraints...

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:51.669
internal combustion system

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.475
producing lethal levels
of carbon monoxide.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.074
Hmm. L stand corrected.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:02:00.644
This may be just what you need
to get you back to Sick Bay.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.882
L guess l should have known
this wouldn't interest you.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:03.889
It's too much fun.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.221
This isn't about fun, Mr. Paris.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.920
Serving in Sick Bay
is a privilege.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.428
L'd expect you to realize that.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.157
Oh, l do.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.755
L'll be there.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.699
Soon.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:22.541
Lieutenant Paris, report
to the Bridge immediately.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.603
L'm on my way.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.348
Somebody call for a driver?

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.049
Take your station, Tom.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.285
Anything on scans, Harry?

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.419
L'm picking up
another spatial distortion

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.588
2,000 kilometers away.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.597
Source?

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:45.757
L have no idea.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.062
It looks like space
is folding in on itself.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.126
Shields to full.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.642
It's an alien vessel.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.667
One occupant aboard.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.008
Captain, it looks like

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.106
that ship is being powered
by a coaxial warp drive.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.844
Coaxial what?

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.442
Lt's a hypothetical
propulsion system.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.386
Starfleet engineers have been
dreaming about it for years.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.448
In theory, it can literally
fold the fabric of space

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.858
allowing a ship
to travel instantaneously

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.226
across huge distances.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.293
The alien warp drive
is overloading.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:26.863
In theory,
a coaxial drive explosion...

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.305
could collapse space

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:31.105
within a radius
of a billion kilometers.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.874
In theory.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.143
Well, let's keep theory
from becoming reality.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.479
Red Alert.

00:05:30.695 --> 00:05:32.219
Scan the vessel.

00:05:32.263 --> 00:05:34.458
Can we beam the pilot out?

00:05:34.499 --> 00:05:35.966
Too much interference.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.729
That ship's about had it,
Captain.

00:05:37.769 --> 00:05:39.794
The coaxial core is breaching.

00:05:39.837 --> 00:05:42.863
We should vacate this area
of space at once.

00:05:42.907 --> 00:05:44.738
We can't just
leave him like this.

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:46.107
Try one more hail.

00:05:47.145 --> 00:05:49.670
Nothing.
Maybe he's ignoring us.

00:05:49.714 --> 00:05:50.908
Or maybe he's unconscious.

00:05:50.948 --> 00:05:52.210
We've got to do something.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.308
Suggestions?

00:05:57.789 --> 00:05:59.950
A symmetric warp field.

00:05:59.991 --> 00:06:01.720
That should contain
any instabilities

00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:03.522
in his space folding core.

00:06:03.561 --> 00:06:04.823
How can you be sure?

00:06:04.862 --> 00:06:07.763
Advanced subspace geometry.

00:06:07.799 --> 00:06:09.266
It's the one course
at the Academy

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.767
where l actually paid attention.

00:06:10.802 --> 00:06:13.327
We'll tractor him in
to kill his momentum

00:06:13.371 --> 00:06:15.669
and generate a warp field
around his ship.

00:06:15.707 --> 00:06:18.175
His flight path is erratic.

00:06:18.209 --> 00:06:20.143
We'd be risking collision.

00:06:20.178 --> 00:06:22.237
Captain, l can make this work.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.872
Do it.

00:06:31.456 --> 00:06:34.016
Passing through
the residual folds in space.

00:06:34.058 --> 00:06:36.253
Steady.

00:06:39.731 --> 00:06:41.699
Got him!

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:44.725
L've extended our warp field
around his vessel.

00:06:44.769 --> 00:06:46.828
His core is powering down.

00:06:46.871 --> 00:06:48.395
Nice flying, Tom.

00:06:48.439 --> 00:06:50.930
My pleasure.

00:06:50.975 --> 00:06:53.170
We're finally receiving a hail.

00:06:53.211 --> 00:06:55.406
Open a channel.

00:06:55.446 --> 00:06:58.381
Captain Janeway of the
Federation Starship Voyager.

00:06:58.416 --> 00:07:00.008
Do you need medical attention?

00:07:00.051 --> 00:07:01.279
L'm fine, Captain.

00:07:01.319 --> 00:07:03.787
Unfortunately, my ship is not.

00:07:03.821 --> 00:07:07.052
If you need to make repairs,
we might be able to help.

00:07:07.091 --> 00:07:08.888
That's very generous.

00:07:08.926 --> 00:07:11.622
We'll beam you aboard
in a few minutes. Stand by.

00:07:11.662 --> 00:07:13.027
Thank you.

00:07:13.064 --> 00:07:14.895
Tuvok.

00:07:20.304 --> 00:07:21.794
Energize.

00:07:27.145 --> 00:07:28.112
Welcome.

00:07:28.146 --> 00:07:29.408
Captain.

00:07:29.447 --> 00:07:31.745
L know you put yourselves
in danger to rescue me.

00:07:31.783 --> 00:07:32.772
L want to thank you.

00:07:32.817 --> 00:07:34.341
L'm glad we could help.

00:07:34.385 --> 00:07:37.183
L was so eager
to test my new engine,

00:07:37.221 --> 00:07:39.655
l pushed it beyond its limits.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:43.592
Coaxial warp doesn't seem to be
the smoothest way to travel.

00:07:43.628 --> 00:07:46.756
It's a violent procedure,
but it allows a ship

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:49.266
to travel through space
at incredible speeds.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.631
Considering the dangers,

00:07:50.668 --> 00:07:53.159
this method of travel
hardly seems logical.

00:07:53.204 --> 00:07:55.035
That's probably true,

00:07:55.072 --> 00:07:57.267
but if l were
worrying about danger,

00:07:57.308 --> 00:07:58.832
l wouldn't have
become a test pilot.

00:07:58.876 --> 00:08:00.138
Where are you from?

00:08:00.178 --> 00:08:02.305
The fourth planet
in the Benthan system.

00:08:02.346 --> 00:08:04.906
That's about 20
light-years from here.

00:08:04.949 --> 00:08:07.042
L'll speak to my engineers
about helping you with repairs.

00:08:07.084 --> 00:08:10.383
Without your coaxial drive,
it's a long way home.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.022
Come in.

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:25.435
L'd like to ask you a favor.

00:08:25.536 --> 00:08:27.970
L need a change of pace.

00:08:28.005 --> 00:08:29.836
L'd like to help Steth
repair his ship.

00:08:29.874 --> 00:08:31.842
This isn't a good time to ask.

00:08:33.377 --> 00:08:34.435
What do you mean?

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:36.413
L've been reading a report
from the Doctor.

00:08:36.447 --> 00:08:38.210
You didn't show up today.

00:08:38.249 --> 00:08:41.446
Well, l was a little busy
this morning...

00:08:41.486 --> 00:08:43.954
saving someone's life,
as l recall.

00:08:43.988 --> 00:08:45.751
Is there something wrong, Tom?

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.382
Anything bothering you?

00:08:47.425 --> 00:08:49.450
Nothing is wrong.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.050
Since when is not
wanting to spend

00:08:51.095 --> 00:08:53.063
time with the Doctor
a capital offense?

00:08:53.097 --> 00:08:54.462
You'd have to throw
the whole crew

00:08:54.532 --> 00:08:55.658
in the brig for that one.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.830
Maybe. L was just wondering if
there's something on your mind.

00:08:59.871 --> 00:09:01.463
You're showing up
for your duty shifts,

00:09:01.506 --> 00:09:02.803
you do what's required,

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:04.831
but your heart doesn't seem
to be in it.

00:09:04.876 --> 00:09:06.969
You seem preoccupied.

00:09:07.011 --> 00:09:11.209
Like l said,
l think l need a change of pace.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:13.717
You're a different man

00:09:13.751 --> 00:09:15.651
from the one that came
on board four years ago.

00:09:15.686 --> 00:09:18.416
You've taken charge of your
life, turned yourself around.

00:09:18.523 --> 00:09:20.684
L'd hate to see you ruin it.

00:09:23.995 --> 00:09:25.656
L won't.

00:09:25.696 --> 00:09:29.655
With your permission,
l'll report to Sick Bay.

00:09:31.068 --> 00:09:33.366
Permission denied.

00:09:35.339 --> 00:09:37.534
Report to Steth's ship instead.

00:09:37.575 --> 00:09:39.338
Assist in the repairs.

00:09:39.377 --> 00:09:41.504
We need our best man on the job.

00:09:49.387 --> 00:09:50.786
And on my way back,

00:09:50.821 --> 00:09:52.550
l made the mistake
of flying the prototype

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:54.581
through restricted
Entaban territory.

00:09:54.625 --> 00:09:55.592
And?

00:09:55.626 --> 00:09:57.184
And, uh...

00:09:57.228 --> 00:09:59.458
the Entabans weren't
too pleased to see me.

00:10:00.865 --> 00:10:03.698
L limped back to the engineers
on Benthos with phaser holes

00:10:03.734 --> 00:10:06.760
through their brand-new
exatanium fuselage.

00:10:06.804 --> 00:10:08.271
L think they would
have been happier

00:10:08.306 --> 00:10:09.967
to see phaser holes through me.

00:10:11.676 --> 00:10:16.477
When l was 16, l followed
an ancient human custom.

00:10:16.581 --> 00:10:19.209
L took my father's shuttle
out for a joyride

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:21.775
and proceeded
to fry all the relays.

00:10:21.819 --> 00:10:25.084
L'm guessing he wasn't happy
about getting it back.

00:10:25.122 --> 00:10:26.646
Actually, he didn't.

00:10:26.691 --> 00:10:27.658
As far as l know,

00:10:27.692 --> 00:10:29.717
it's still at the bottom
of Lake Tahoe.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:30.920
Here it is.

00:10:30.962 --> 00:10:32.862
The coaxial induction drive.

00:10:32.897 --> 00:10:36.060
It draws in subatomic particles
and reconfigures

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.328
their internal geometries.

00:10:37.368 --> 00:10:39.632
And this is what makes
folding space possible?

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.228
At least in spurts.

00:10:41.272 --> 00:10:42.739
Unfortunately,

00:10:42.773 --> 00:10:45.936
particle instabilities
keep overloading my engines,

00:10:45.977 --> 00:10:47.444
but l'm going to make it work.

00:10:47.478 --> 00:10:48.775
L have to keep in motion.

00:10:48.813 --> 00:10:52.180
L don't like the thought
of settling down...

00:10:52.216 --> 00:10:55.777
too many new ships to drive,
too many intriguing women.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:57.651
Yeah. L guess so.

00:10:57.688 --> 00:10:59.383
When l get this ship back,

00:10:59.423 --> 00:11:01.152
l'm going to be
doing the first test

00:11:01.192 --> 00:11:03.319
on a new Mithran-class fighter.

00:11:03.361 --> 00:11:05.022
L'm told it's more advanced

00:11:05.062 --> 00:11:07.053
than any warship
in the Quadrant.

00:11:07.098 --> 00:11:08.998
Why don't you come with me?

00:11:09.033 --> 00:11:11.467
We'd have a great time.

00:11:11.569 --> 00:11:13.434
You can meet up
with Voyager afterwards.

00:11:17.174 --> 00:11:18.641
L-l'd love to do that.

00:11:18.676 --> 00:11:20.473
It sounds very exciting...

00:11:22.046 --> 00:11:24.879
but l have
responsibilities here,

00:11:24.915 --> 00:11:26.849
people who count on me

00:11:26.884 --> 00:11:29.352
and B'Elanna would be furious.

00:11:32.657 --> 00:11:34.386
B'Elanna.

00:11:36.494 --> 00:11:37.961
L have to go.

00:11:54.211 --> 00:11:55.872
So, you started without me.

00:11:55.913 --> 00:11:58.507
L finished without you.

00:11:58.616 --> 00:12:00.243
You're a little late.

00:12:00.284 --> 00:12:02.548
Uh, sorry.

00:12:02.586 --> 00:12:05.282
L was helping Steth
repair his ship.

00:12:05.322 --> 00:12:07.449
How's it going?

00:12:07.558 --> 00:12:10.686
Um... pretty slow.

00:12:10.728 --> 00:12:12.093
We're both stuck
on how to prevent

00:12:12.129 --> 00:12:14.927
the particle overloads
in his propulsion system.

00:12:14.965 --> 00:12:17.729
Have you tried
an isokinetic containment field?

00:12:17.768 --> 00:12:21.465
Yeah. That's the first thing
we tried.

00:12:21.539 --> 00:12:24.007
How long do you think these
repairs are going to take?

00:12:24.041 --> 00:12:26.066
L don't know.

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:29.876
L was just hoping
that maybe you could help me

00:12:29.914 --> 00:12:31.882
recalibrate
the plasma manifolds tonight.

00:12:31.916 --> 00:12:36.250
Uh... I, uh...

00:12:36.287 --> 00:12:38.721
l probably should go help Steth.

00:12:43.227 --> 00:12:45.024
Tom, is there something wrong?

00:12:46.664 --> 00:12:48.131
Why are you interrogating me?

00:12:48.165 --> 00:12:50.030
L didn't think l was.

00:12:50.067 --> 00:12:51.694
It sounds more like you
want me to account

00:12:51.736 --> 00:12:53.260
for every minute
that l'm not with you.

00:12:53.304 --> 00:12:54.862
That's ridiculous.

00:12:54.905 --> 00:12:56.099
Can't l have
some time to myself?

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:58.199
Can't l do what l want
without having to report

00:12:58.242 --> 00:12:59.436
every detail of it to you?

00:12:59.477 --> 00:13:01.638
Tom, you can do
whatever you want.

00:13:01.679 --> 00:13:04.204
L just wanted to know
if there was something wrong.

00:13:04.248 --> 00:13:06.216
L mean, lately,
you've been canceling dates,

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:08.411
you hide out for hours
in the holodeck...

00:13:08.452 --> 00:13:09.783
l am not hiding anything.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:10.809
That is ridiculous.

00:13:10.855 --> 00:13:12.322
Is it?

00:13:12.356 --> 00:13:14.187
You haven't even told me
what holodeck program this is

00:13:14.225 --> 00:13:15.214
that has you so fascinated.

00:13:16.794 --> 00:13:19.456
"The Dancing Girls
of Ninipia Prime."

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:20.929
Lt's very entertaining.

00:13:20.965 --> 00:13:22.262
Very funny.

00:13:22.299 --> 00:13:23.630
You're overreacting.

00:13:23.667 --> 00:13:26.465
L am not overreacting.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.834
There is obviously
something going on

00:13:28.873 --> 00:13:30.306
and you're refusing to admit it.

00:13:30.341 --> 00:13:32.138
Good evening, Lieutenants.

00:13:32.176 --> 00:13:33.643
L see you don't have
your dinner yet, Tom.

00:13:33.677 --> 00:13:34.666
Can l get you something?

00:13:34.712 --> 00:13:35.804
- L'm really not hungry.
- Excuse me.

00:13:35.846 --> 00:13:37.643
Are you going to talk to me
about this?

00:13:37.681 --> 00:13:39.979
Because if you're not, l don't
want to sit here anymore.

00:13:40.017 --> 00:13:41.575
If you can carry on
an adult conversation

00:13:41.619 --> 00:13:42.916
without all the histrionics...

00:13:42.953 --> 00:13:44.511
Good night, Tom.

00:14:14.285 --> 00:14:17.721
Computer, run
a DNA stability analysis.

00:14:17.755 --> 00:14:20.952
How long before my genome
reverts to its previous form?

00:14:20.991 --> 00:14:24.950
Time to reversion:
Three hours, 13 minutes.

00:14:24.995 --> 00:14:27.623
Complete genome recovery
is imminent.

00:14:36.906 --> 00:14:39.568
So l was lying in bed
last night when it hit me.

00:14:39.608 --> 00:14:42.270
What you need is a carburetor.

00:14:42.311 --> 00:14:43.573
A carburetor?

00:14:43.612 --> 00:14:46.638
Yes. It's a device
that's hundreds of years old.

00:14:46.682 --> 00:14:48.309
L can't believe l didn't
think of it yesterday.

00:14:48.351 --> 00:14:50.216
Wait. Hundreds of years old?

00:14:50.252 --> 00:14:52.243
Surely that couldn't be
of any use to us now.

00:14:52.288 --> 00:14:54.279
It all goes back to basics.

00:14:54.323 --> 00:14:56.985
You would be surprised
at how often l find solutions

00:14:57.026 --> 00:15:00.792
to 24th century problems
in 20th century technology.

00:15:02.231 --> 00:15:06.258
Computer, access Paris program
Alpha 1: "Grease Monkey."

00:15:07.269 --> 00:15:08.702
Grease monkey?

00:15:08.738 --> 00:15:10.569
Mechanic lingo.

00:15:14.643 --> 00:15:16.838
A car's engine can't
run on pure fuel,

00:15:16.879 --> 00:15:18.574
so the carburetor supplies it

00:15:18.614 --> 00:15:20.548
with a mixture
of vaporized fuel and air.

00:15:20.583 --> 00:15:21.777
And you think we need

00:15:21.817 --> 00:15:24.945
a device like that
to dilute the particle stream

00:15:24.987 --> 00:15:26.648
as it enters the coaxial drive.

00:15:26.689 --> 00:15:28.156
Exactly,

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.452
and a spare polaric modulator

00:15:29.525 --> 00:15:31.755
from Voyager's impulse drive
should do the trick.

00:15:31.794 --> 00:15:33.318
Subatomic dilution!

00:15:33.362 --> 00:15:35.853
Oh! Lt never would have
occurred to me.

00:15:35.898 --> 00:15:37.456
L think you've solved it.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:40.094
Well, we can run a few
simulations on the holodeck

00:15:40.136 --> 00:15:41.626
before we actually try it.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.661
Oh... l owe you a lot.

00:15:43.706 --> 00:15:45.936
Well, you can thank
my lucky toolbox.

00:15:45.975 --> 00:15:48.136
It's gotten me out of hot water
more than once.

00:15:48.177 --> 00:15:49.235
Mmm.

00:15:51.747 --> 00:15:55.012
You're lucky to be stationed
on a ship like this.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.780
Replicators to feed
and clothe you

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:01.051
holotechnology
to cater to every whim,

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.854
hallways filled with women.

00:16:03.893 --> 00:16:05.019
Yeah.

00:16:06.061 --> 00:16:07.289
It's great.

00:16:07.329 --> 00:16:08.853
Well, you don't sound convinced.

00:16:08.898 --> 00:16:11.366
Aren't you happy here?

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.526
Of course l'm happy.

00:16:12.568 --> 00:16:14.331
L'm very happy.

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.429
L mean... l pilot

00:16:16.539 --> 00:16:18.905
one of the most advanced ships
in Starfleet.

00:16:18.941 --> 00:16:20.704
L have a beautiful girlfriend.

00:16:20.743 --> 00:16:22.074
L'm respected.

00:16:22.111 --> 00:16:26.047
L have everything
that l've ever wanted.

00:16:26.081 --> 00:16:27.912
You're lucky.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:31.386
You're part of a family,
part of a structure.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.911
You have rules to guide you.

00:16:33.956 --> 00:16:36.356
You don't have to worry
about making a lot of choices.

00:16:36.392 --> 00:16:37.984
L usually go to bed at night

00:16:38.027 --> 00:16:40.359
not knowing what the next day
has in store...

00:16:40.396 --> 00:16:42.762
what trouble l might get into.

00:16:44.133 --> 00:16:46.328
You don't have to worry
about those things.

00:16:46.368 --> 00:16:48.063
You're very settled.

00:16:49.338 --> 00:16:52.034
L remember those days.

00:16:52.074 --> 00:16:54.634
L used to be a lot like you...

00:16:54.677 --> 00:16:57.874
going anywhere...

00:16:57.913 --> 00:16:59.847
doing whatever l wanted...

00:16:59.882 --> 00:17:02.578
making my own rules.

00:17:03.752 --> 00:17:06.380
Well, then there's hope
for me yet.

00:17:06.422 --> 00:17:08.890
Maybe someday
l'll settle down, too,

00:17:08.924 --> 00:17:13.861
but... for now...
l prefer to stay on the move.

00:17:15.264 --> 00:17:18.233
Sometimes... l wish
that's what l was doing.

00:17:19.802 --> 00:17:21.667
Things'll turn around for you.

00:17:21.704 --> 00:17:24.696
L've always found
that change is inevitable.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.038
It comes when you
least expect it.

00:17:28.277 --> 00:17:29.801
Yeah, l suppose.

00:17:29.845 --> 00:17:30.937
Now, are we ready

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.540
to try this carburetor
idea on my ship?

00:17:33.582 --> 00:17:35.447
Just give me five more minutes
to finish up here

00:17:35.551 --> 00:17:36.643
and l'll be right with you.

00:17:36.685 --> 00:17:37.777
Five minutes.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.118
And, Tom...

00:17:40.155 --> 00:17:42.248
don't dismiss the suggestion

00:17:42.291 --> 00:17:46.318
l made... about coming with me
to fly the new ship.

00:17:46.362 --> 00:17:50.230
It might be fun to escape
the shackles for a while.

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.498
Hmm.

00:18:26.702 --> 00:18:28.169
Computer, access all files

00:18:28.203 --> 00:18:30.137
pertaining
to Lieutenant Tom Paris.

00:18:30.172 --> 00:18:32.868
Download into Memory Core Alpha.

00:18:32.908 --> 00:18:36.139
Please enter authorization code.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:39.208
Access granted.

00:18:39.248 --> 00:18:41.512
Commencing download.

00:18:57.666 --> 00:18:59.429
Hello.

00:18:59.468 --> 00:19:01.163
L'm Steth...

00:19:01.203 --> 00:19:02.898
a guest of your Captain.

00:19:02.938 --> 00:19:05.304
L have been apprised
of your presence on Voyager.

00:19:05.341 --> 00:19:08.174
You are not authorized
to access the ship's computers.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.677
You must be Seven of Nine.

00:19:09.712 --> 00:19:10.804
That is correct.

00:19:10.846 --> 00:19:11.972
Tom mentioned you.

00:19:12.014 --> 00:19:14.915
He thinks
you're extremely intelligent.

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:16.315
Lieutenant Paris' opinion of me

00:19:16.352 --> 00:19:18.377
is irrelevant
to your being in this room.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:21.184
Well, uh... Tom felt
we needed some files

00:19:21.223 --> 00:19:23.418
for polaric modulators,

00:19:23.459 --> 00:19:25.950
but he was called away
before we could access them.

00:19:25.995 --> 00:19:28.054
L thought l'd find them
myself and help out.

00:19:28.097 --> 00:19:29.428
You were mistaken.

00:19:29.531 --> 00:19:31.396
He must be present
to download these files.

00:19:31.433 --> 00:19:33.424
Oh, l'm about to meet
him at the holodeck.

00:19:33.535 --> 00:19:35.059
We can find the files there.

00:19:35.104 --> 00:19:38.369
Voyager's hierarchy is complex.

00:19:38.407 --> 00:19:40.807
See that you familiarize
yourself with it.

00:19:40.843 --> 00:19:42.367
Good advice.

00:19:42.411 --> 00:19:44.003
L'll do that.

00:19:50.986 --> 00:19:54.683
Captain's Log, Stardate 51762.4.

00:19:54.723 --> 00:19:56.452
The repairs
to Steth's coaxial drive

00:19:56.492 --> 00:19:59.950
have been completed
well ahead of schedule.

00:19:59.995 --> 00:20:02.429
Everything here looks good.

00:20:02.464 --> 00:20:04.898
Just give me one more second
to check

00:20:04.933 --> 00:20:06.264
the flow-field parameters.

00:20:06.301 --> 00:20:07.290
Go ahead.

00:20:26.855 --> 00:20:28.584
It's my box wrench.

00:20:28.624 --> 00:20:30.489
L've been looking
all over for this.

00:20:30.592 --> 00:20:32.184
L know. L should've asked you,
Tom,

00:20:32.227 --> 00:20:35.458
but l needed it
for an experiment.

00:20:37.433 --> 00:20:40.197
To, uh... check
your new carburetor?

00:20:40.235 --> 00:20:41.429
Not quite.

00:20:42.838 --> 00:20:45.102
You're the first humans l've met

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:47.404
and that wrench had
enough cellular residue

00:20:47.443 --> 00:20:49.104
on it for me to check your DNA.

00:20:50.479 --> 00:20:52.003
L have good news.

00:20:54.183 --> 00:20:56.242
We're compatible.

00:21:07.663 --> 00:21:10.131
Consider this a favor.

00:21:10.165 --> 00:21:14.158
L know how unhappy you've been
with this dreary, settled life,

00:21:14.203 --> 00:21:16.603
so l'm taking it off your hands.

00:21:16.638 --> 00:21:19.471
L'm betting there's still
some fun to be had here.

00:21:19.575 --> 00:21:22.476
Voyager is a great ship, Tom.

00:21:22.511 --> 00:21:25.309
L'll take good care of it.

00:21:35.157 --> 00:21:36.784
Sorry l'm late.

00:21:36.825 --> 00:21:39.555
We were beginning to wonder
if you were ever coming back.

00:21:42.765 --> 00:21:44.699
His ship is powering engines.

00:21:54.176 --> 00:21:55.803
Something wrong, Tom?

00:21:58.213 --> 00:21:59.805
Lt's nothing.

00:22:06.922 --> 00:22:09.356
L'm just really going
to miss that guy.

00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:25.229
Mind if l join you?

00:22:25.273 --> 00:22:26.638
Not at all...

00:22:26.674 --> 00:22:27.936
Commander.

00:22:27.975 --> 00:22:29.237
"Chakotay" will do, Tom.

00:22:29.277 --> 00:22:31.370
You don't have to carry
this "rules" thing too far.

00:22:31.412 --> 00:22:34.404
L've been discussing
your engineering report

00:22:34.448 --> 00:22:35.642
with the Captain.

00:22:35.683 --> 00:22:36.980
She was wondering
if we could implement

00:22:37.018 --> 00:22:39.282
some of Steth's technology
here on Voyager.

00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:41.220
Really?

00:22:41.255 --> 00:22:43.587
We thought maybe
you could start on a shuttle.

00:22:43.624 --> 00:22:45.455
Do you think you can do it?

00:22:45.493 --> 00:22:48.121
L'm sure l can.

00:22:48.162 --> 00:22:51.495
Great. You can start right after
you finish with the Doctor.

00:22:51.566 --> 00:22:53.625
The Doctor?

00:22:53.668 --> 00:22:55.397
He needs your help in Sick Bay.

00:22:55.436 --> 00:22:56.733
L told him you'd be there.

00:22:56.771 --> 00:22:58.739
Of course.

00:23:03.578 --> 00:23:04.545
Lieutenant.

00:23:04.579 --> 00:23:05.568
Hi.

00:23:44.251 --> 00:23:46.776
L know you've been
avoiding the Doctor,

00:23:46.821 --> 00:23:49.722
but don't tell me you've
forgotten where Sick Bay is.

00:23:49.757 --> 00:23:52.783
Oh... not yet.

00:23:52.827 --> 00:23:54.624
L was just trying to figure out

00:23:54.662 --> 00:23:56.596
if there's
a more efficient route

00:23:56.631 --> 00:23:58.360
between Sick Bay
and my quarters.

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:01.568
L didn't realize you were
that eager to get there.

00:24:03.270 --> 00:24:05.397
So tell me...
are they ready yet?

00:24:05.439 --> 00:24:08.374
Uh... not yet.

00:24:08.409 --> 00:24:09.808
But they will be soon.

00:24:09.844 --> 00:24:11.038
Great.

00:24:11.078 --> 00:24:12.909
Hey, let me know
if you have any problems.

00:24:12.947 --> 00:24:14.915
Polyduranide
can be tough to replicate.

00:24:14.949 --> 00:24:16.439
Oh, it sure can be.

00:24:16.484 --> 00:24:19.749
L can't wait to get my hands
around one of those clubs.

00:24:19.787 --> 00:24:21.652
Ensign Kaplan won't
know what hit her.

00:24:21.689 --> 00:24:24.055
What?

00:24:24.091 --> 00:24:25.854
We're going to play golf
with her.

00:24:25.893 --> 00:24:28.191
We scheduled a rematch,
remember?

00:24:28.229 --> 00:24:29.457
Oh, of course.

00:24:29.563 --> 00:24:31.087
L can't wait.

00:24:31.132 --> 00:24:32.622
Have you been working
on your putting?

00:24:32.667 --> 00:24:34.396
You missed both those
two-footers last time.

00:24:34.435 --> 00:24:36.130
L won't let it happen again.

00:24:36.170 --> 00:24:38.195
All right.

00:24:38.239 --> 00:24:39.297
Give the Doc my best.

00:24:39.340 --> 00:24:40.329
L will...

00:24:42.276 --> 00:24:44.301
if l ever find him.

00:24:48.582 --> 00:24:51.073
You're early, Mr. Paris.

00:24:51.118 --> 00:24:53.143
L see some good
came from my report

00:24:53.187 --> 00:24:54.484
to Commander Chakotay.

00:24:54.555 --> 00:24:57.422
Let's put these extra
few minutes to good use.

00:24:57.458 --> 00:24:59.892
Begin with a thorough
bio-bed diagnostic.

00:24:59.927 --> 00:25:02.327
L want you to recalibrate
each physiosensor,

00:25:02.363 --> 00:25:03.421
making sure to enter

00:25:03.531 --> 00:25:05.431
every metabolic
referent precisely.

00:25:05.533 --> 00:25:06.431
Okay.

00:25:06.534 --> 00:25:07.694
When you're through with that,

00:25:07.735 --> 00:25:09.032
run a protein
structure analysis

00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:11.595
and then continue your review
of the 37 steps

00:25:11.639 --> 00:25:14.233
of a cardiopulmonary
reconstruction procedure.

00:25:14.275 --> 00:25:16.004
L'll leave you
to your bio-beds.

00:25:19.980 --> 00:25:22.448
Did you forget to disengage
the scan emitters?

00:25:22.483 --> 00:25:24.474
Sorry.

00:25:25.753 --> 00:25:27.778
Mr. Paris!

00:25:29.290 --> 00:25:30.382
L don't know what's wrong.

00:25:30.424 --> 00:25:31.391
L realize

00:25:31.425 --> 00:25:33.620
it's complicated,
but you must try again.

00:25:33.661 --> 00:25:36.027
Actually,
l'm not feeling so well.

00:25:36.063 --> 00:25:38.759
How fortunate you're
already in Sick Bay.

00:25:38.799 --> 00:25:40.027
L'll run a few scans.

00:25:40.067 --> 00:25:42.194
Uh, no, no, Doc.
That's all right.

00:25:42.236 --> 00:25:44.295
To be perfectly honest with you,

00:25:44.338 --> 00:25:48.968
uh... this is
so frustrating for me.

00:25:49.009 --> 00:25:51.637
L usually pick things up
a lot faster than this.

00:25:51.679 --> 00:25:53.476
You're here to learn,
Mr. Paris.

00:25:53.514 --> 00:25:55.482
It will get easier with time.

00:25:55.516 --> 00:25:57.746
Well, that's easy
for you to say.

00:25:57.785 --> 00:25:58.945
Excuse me?

00:25:58.986 --> 00:26:01.352
Well, no offense, Doctor, but...

00:26:01.388 --> 00:26:03.356
you were programmed
to be a medical genius.

00:26:03.390 --> 00:26:05.358
Things always come easy to you.

00:26:05.392 --> 00:26:07.724
Me, l'm just a pilot,
a... grease monkey.

00:26:07.762 --> 00:26:09.923
And as hard as l might try

00:26:09.964 --> 00:26:13.024
to become
a better assistant to you,

00:26:13.067 --> 00:26:14.261
it's clear to me now

00:26:14.301 --> 00:26:17.168
that l'll never be half
the healer that you are.

00:26:18.272 --> 00:26:20.069
Do you mean to tell me

00:26:20.107 --> 00:26:23.201
you've been trying
to live up to my standards?

00:26:24.812 --> 00:26:26.279
L'm afraid l have.

00:26:27.515 --> 00:26:29.142
It all makes sense now.

00:26:29.183 --> 00:26:31.048
The misplaced aggression,

00:26:31.085 --> 00:26:33.918
the shirking
of responsibilities...

00:26:33.954 --> 00:26:37.856
all classic signs
of an inferiority complex.

00:26:40.027 --> 00:26:42.996
L had no idea
my superior abilities

00:26:43.030 --> 00:26:45.464
were affecting your psyche
so strongly.

00:26:45.566 --> 00:26:47.761
Take the rest of the day off.

00:26:47.802 --> 00:26:49.702
Reflect on your strengths.

00:26:49.737 --> 00:26:51.796
Realize your worth.

00:26:54.041 --> 00:26:56.407
L'll do that, Doctor.

00:26:57.645 --> 00:26:59.078
Thank you.

00:27:19.733 --> 00:27:20.791
B'Elanna.

00:27:20.835 --> 00:27:23.395
What do you think you're doing?

00:27:23.437 --> 00:27:25.132
Putting.

00:27:25.172 --> 00:27:26.434
In my quarters?

00:27:26.540 --> 00:27:29.008
L can't putt in your quarters?

00:27:29.043 --> 00:27:30.305
No.

00:27:30.344 --> 00:27:31.675
Since when?

00:27:33.681 --> 00:27:35.046
Tom...

00:27:38.285 --> 00:27:39.877
what is this?

00:27:39.920 --> 00:27:42.115
That is...

00:27:42.156 --> 00:27:43.248
a sand wedge.

00:27:43.290 --> 00:27:45.588
It's used for getting
out of traps.

00:27:45.626 --> 00:27:47.787
Why is it here?

00:27:47.828 --> 00:27:49.455
L replicated it for you.

00:27:49.530 --> 00:27:51.589
L thought we could play
a little game of golf

00:27:51.632 --> 00:27:53.793
on the holodeck before dinner.

00:27:53.834 --> 00:27:58.032
So this is your idea
of an adult conversation?

00:28:00.207 --> 00:28:03.040
L don't know what you
are trying to accomplish

00:28:03.077 --> 00:28:04.567
with this little stunt,

00:28:04.612 --> 00:28:07.513
but let me assure you,
it is not working.

00:28:07.548 --> 00:28:10.176
L am sorry if you are bored
because Steth is gone,

00:28:10.217 --> 00:28:12.412
but that doesn't mean
that you can just walk in here

00:28:12.453 --> 00:28:14.614
and pretend like you haven't
been shutting me out.

00:28:16.624 --> 00:28:19.354
You're being a little hard
on Steth.

00:28:19.393 --> 00:28:23.022
If it wasn't for him,
l wouldn't be here right now.

00:28:23.063 --> 00:28:25.361
Really?

00:28:25.399 --> 00:28:31.099
L mentioned to him that we were
having some problems

00:28:31.138 --> 00:28:34.107
and he urged me to...

00:28:34.141 --> 00:28:36.268
come and talk to you,

00:28:36.310 --> 00:28:38.835
to try to work things out,

00:28:38.879 --> 00:28:41.643
to admit l was wrong.

00:28:43.751 --> 00:28:46.777
L made a mistake, B'Elanna,

00:28:46.820 --> 00:28:48.947
and l'm sorry.

00:28:53.627 --> 00:28:56.824
L won't shut you out anymore.

00:28:56.864 --> 00:29:01.528
In fact, l went to the Doctor
and begged

00:29:01.568 --> 00:29:04.059
to be excused from my duties.

00:29:04.104 --> 00:29:07.699
L realize it's only
a few extra hours,

00:29:07.741 --> 00:29:10.209
but they're hours
l want to spend with you.

00:29:20.988 --> 00:29:25.891
Steth... turned out to be
a positive influence on you.

00:29:57.391 --> 00:29:58.949
Computer, where...

00:30:02.262 --> 00:30:04.423
Com-Computer, where are we?

00:30:04.465 --> 00:30:10.335
Navigation matrix 1711,
the Kotaba Expanse.

00:30:10.371 --> 00:30:11.998
Coaxial leap complete.

00:30:12.039 --> 00:30:13.768
How far are we from Voyager?

00:30:17.311 --> 00:30:20.974
Computer, lock in Voyager's
last known coordinates

00:30:21.015 --> 00:30:23.609
and activate
differential induction drive.

00:30:23.650 --> 00:30:25.982
Unable to execute command.

00:30:26.020 --> 00:30:27.487
Why not?

00:30:27.588 --> 00:30:30.580
The differential induction drive
has been secured.

00:30:30.624 --> 00:30:32.751
A security access code
is required

00:30:32.793 --> 00:30:34.590
to implement the coaxial leap.

00:30:39.133 --> 00:30:41.294
This is Commander Avik
of the Benthan Guard.

00:30:41.335 --> 00:30:42.802
We're taking you into custody.

00:30:42.836 --> 00:30:45.134
Prepare to surrender the vessel
to us at once.

00:30:45.172 --> 00:30:46.696
Benthan?

00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:50.733
L need a second to explain,
Commander.

00:30:50.778 --> 00:30:52.143
L'm not who you think...

00:30:52.179 --> 00:30:54.875
We do not negotiate
with thieves.

00:30:55.849 --> 00:30:58.317
No... you don't understand!

00:30:58.352 --> 00:31:01.048
I-I need this ship
to get back to Voyager.

00:31:01.088 --> 00:31:04.683
Surrender the vessel peacefully
or we will use force.

00:31:22.942 --> 00:31:25.376
Why is everybody trying
to shoot me today?

00:31:25.411 --> 00:31:26.639
You know what l'm here for.

00:31:26.679 --> 00:31:28.738
L don't know
what you're talking about.

00:31:28.781 --> 00:31:30.078
Who are you?

00:31:30.116 --> 00:31:31.583
L'm Steth.

00:31:31.617 --> 00:31:32.811
What?

00:31:32.852 --> 00:31:34.080
Look at me.

00:31:34.120 --> 00:31:36.213
You did wear this body
for nearly a year

00:31:36.255 --> 00:31:38.985
before you switched it
with mine.

00:31:39.025 --> 00:31:41.118
That's my body you're in now.

00:31:41.160 --> 00:31:42.787
L want it back.

00:31:42.828 --> 00:31:44.921
Bear with me
for... for a second.

00:31:44.964 --> 00:31:48.331
We have more in common
than you might think.

00:31:56.542 --> 00:31:58.271
This better be good, Tom.

00:31:58.311 --> 00:32:01.542
L left Vorik right in the middle
of an EPS recalibration.

00:32:02.748 --> 00:32:04.443
You can thank me later.

00:32:04.517 --> 00:32:07.816
So what's my big surprise?

00:32:07.853 --> 00:32:13.792
What would you say
to 24 glorious hours

00:32:13.826 --> 00:32:17.159
on the famed fourth planet
of the Kendren System?

00:32:17.196 --> 00:32:20.165
You mean the planet where Neelix
is gathering food samples?

00:32:20.199 --> 00:32:23.657
Mm-hmm. L ran a few scans and
found the most incredible beach

00:32:23.703 --> 00:32:25.432
on one
of the smaller continents.

00:32:25.471 --> 00:32:28.634
L replicated
a picnic lunch for us.

00:32:28.674 --> 00:32:31.472
Voyager isn't leaving orbit
until tomorrow.

00:32:31.510 --> 00:32:34.138
We'd have an entire day.

00:32:36.349 --> 00:32:37.907
Only a day?

00:32:39.318 --> 00:32:42.481
Oh, l think that we would need
at least a week.

00:32:42.521 --> 00:32:46.321
Oh, l wish we could,
but we've only got a day.

00:32:48.427 --> 00:32:50.019
You're serious, aren't you?

00:32:50.062 --> 00:32:51.188
Completely.

00:32:51.230 --> 00:32:52.959
Do you know how much trouble
we would be in?

00:32:52.999 --> 00:32:56.435
What could Janeway do,
execute us?

00:32:56.469 --> 00:32:58.130
Tom, l am swamped.

00:32:58.170 --> 00:33:00.229
L can't get away for an hour,
let alone 24.

00:33:00.272 --> 00:33:01.261
B'Elanna...

00:33:01.307 --> 00:33:02.774
l have responsibilities here.

00:33:02.808 --> 00:33:04.002
We both do.

00:33:04.043 --> 00:33:06.170
Responsibilities?
L don't care!

00:33:06.212 --> 00:33:07.804
Tom, you're hurting me.

00:33:07.847 --> 00:33:10.008
You're a real disappointment
to me.

00:33:10.049 --> 00:33:11.243
Do you know that?

00:33:11.283 --> 00:33:13.979
L don't know
what l ever saw in you.

00:33:32.238 --> 00:33:33.728
Seven.

00:33:33.773 --> 00:33:35.104
What brings you here
at this hour?

00:33:38.177 --> 00:33:41.237
We were supposed to meet in
the shuttle bay at 2100 hours.

00:33:41.280 --> 00:33:42.440
Did you forget?

00:33:42.481 --> 00:33:44.278
L did.

00:33:44.316 --> 00:33:46.147
L got so caught up
with my reading,

00:33:46.185 --> 00:33:47.880
l guess it slipped my mind.

00:33:47.920 --> 00:33:49.478
Sorry.

00:33:49.522 --> 00:33:52.013
The capillaries in your eyes
are swollen, Lieutenant,

00:33:52.058 --> 00:33:55.585
and l see signs of vascular
congestion in your cheeks.

00:33:55.628 --> 00:33:57.357
Are you intoxicated?

00:33:57.396 --> 00:33:59.762
No, not at all.

00:33:59.799 --> 00:34:02.893
L was just exploring
the replicator...

00:34:02.935 --> 00:34:04.698
trying some alien beverages.

00:34:04.737 --> 00:34:07.069
Only a few were alcoholic.

00:34:07.106 --> 00:34:10.041
You are not officially off duty
for another 78 minutes.

00:34:10.076 --> 00:34:12.340
L'm on break.

00:34:12.378 --> 00:34:14.369
Would you like to join me?

00:34:14.413 --> 00:34:16.643
L could replicate another
Trakian ale for you.

00:34:16.682 --> 00:34:18.411
That will not be necessary.

00:34:18.451 --> 00:34:20.180
Oh, relax, Seven.

00:34:20.219 --> 00:34:22.949
You're not on the Borg cube
anymore.

00:34:22.988 --> 00:34:24.888
We could finish our work
on the shuttle tomorrow.

00:34:24.924 --> 00:34:27.586
That would be
an inefficient use of our time.

00:34:27.626 --> 00:34:30.151
L will complete the work myself.

00:34:31.197 --> 00:34:32.721
Fine.

00:34:34.533 --> 00:34:36.467
Before l leave,
l would like to know

00:34:36.502 --> 00:34:38.936
why you were reading
the Captain's personal logs.

00:34:41.040 --> 00:34:42.564
L wasn't.

00:34:42.608 --> 00:34:43.905
L saw the padd.

00:34:43.943 --> 00:34:46.173
It was unmistakably
the Captain's logs.

00:34:47.213 --> 00:34:49.443
You're wrong.

00:34:49.482 --> 00:34:51.473
You're... confused.

00:34:51.517 --> 00:34:53.417
You couldn't possibly
have seen anything.

00:34:53.452 --> 00:34:55.420
You know
l possess an eidetic memory.

00:34:55.454 --> 00:34:58.150
L require only seconds
to commit what l see to memory.

00:34:58.190 --> 00:35:00.784
Would you like me to quote
the passage you were reading?

00:35:00.826 --> 00:35:03.386
L'm warning you...
stay out of my way!

00:35:03.429 --> 00:35:05.989
Don't interfere in things
that don't concern you.

00:35:06.031 --> 00:35:07.726
If you bother me again,

00:35:07.767 --> 00:35:10.930
l will make things
very unpleasant for you.

00:35:10.970 --> 00:35:13.666
Remove your hand from my arm.

00:35:13.706 --> 00:35:14.764
Don't be foolish.

00:35:14.807 --> 00:35:16.274
You'll regret it.

00:35:36.195 --> 00:35:37.492
Enter.

00:35:41.100 --> 00:35:43.034
You wanted to see me, Captain.

00:35:45.037 --> 00:35:46.368
Yes.

00:35:48.741 --> 00:35:50.641
L received
a rather disturbing report

00:35:50.676 --> 00:35:53.873
from Seven of Nine regarding
your conduct last night.

00:35:53.913 --> 00:35:56.814
She claims
you were drinking on duty.

00:35:59.318 --> 00:36:00.876
She's mistaken, Captain.

00:36:00.920 --> 00:36:02.046
Don't lie to me, Tom.

00:36:02.087 --> 00:36:03.577
L checked the computers.

00:36:03.622 --> 00:36:06.682
You replicated
five alcoholic beverages

00:36:06.725 --> 00:36:08.283
in the Mess Hall.

00:36:09.762 --> 00:36:12.026
She also said
you threatened her.

00:36:13.132 --> 00:36:14.963
L'm sorry, Captain.

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:16.194
B'Elanna and l had an argument.

00:36:16.235 --> 00:36:17.702
L was upset.

00:36:17.736 --> 00:36:20.534
And is that why you were reading
my personal logs?

00:36:20.573 --> 00:36:22.234
L wasn't.

00:36:22.274 --> 00:36:24.538
Seven recited a passage
l'd written word for word.

00:36:26.378 --> 00:36:28.846
She probably accessed
those files herself.

00:36:28.881 --> 00:36:31.349
Captain, you can't take
the word of a Borg over mine.

00:36:33.385 --> 00:36:35.250
This has to stop, Tom.

00:36:35.287 --> 00:36:37.346
Your conduct lately
has been bizarre

00:36:37.389 --> 00:36:39.084
and l've heard
far too many complaints

00:36:39.124 --> 00:36:40.785
from far too many people
to dismiss it...

00:36:40.826 --> 00:36:42.953
Chakotay, the Doctor,
Seven of Nine.

00:36:42.995 --> 00:36:45.589
They're all worried
about you, and so am I.

00:36:47.066 --> 00:36:49.227
You're right, Captain.
L need some rest.

00:36:49.268 --> 00:36:50.462
L'll go right to my quarters.

00:36:50.502 --> 00:36:52.629
Tom...

00:36:52.671 --> 00:36:55.265
as your Captain
and as your friend...

00:36:55.307 --> 00:36:57.332
l want you to report to Sick Bay
for some tests.

00:36:57.376 --> 00:36:58.775
We have to find out

00:36:58.811 --> 00:37:01.336
if there's something physical
that's causing this behavior.

00:37:01.380 --> 00:37:03.814
This is crazy.

00:37:03.849 --> 00:37:06.317
L don't need any help.

00:37:06.352 --> 00:37:08.217
That's an order.

00:37:10.189 --> 00:37:13.056
Security, l need you
in the ready room now!

00:37:24.270 --> 00:37:25.897
Are you hurt, Captain?

00:37:25.938 --> 00:37:28.372
No. Take him to Sick Bay.

00:37:28.407 --> 00:37:30.875
Keep security with him.

00:37:41.417 --> 00:37:44.716
The coaxial drive will be
on line in a few minutes.

00:37:44.754 --> 00:37:48.451
Good. L've just about overridden
all the lockout commands.

00:37:48.525 --> 00:37:50.117
No offense, but l'd like
to get out of your body

00:37:50.160 --> 00:37:51.422
as soon as possible.

00:37:51.461 --> 00:37:52.894
The alien seems capable

00:37:52.929 --> 00:37:55.329
of some sort
of selective DNA exchange.

00:37:55.365 --> 00:37:56.627
He absorbs new DNA

00:37:56.666 --> 00:37:58.463
while depositing
his current genetic material

00:37:58.568 --> 00:37:59.830
into his victims.

00:37:59.869 --> 00:38:03.100
Let's hope
he can reverse that process.

00:38:04.207 --> 00:38:05.834
That's the last lockout command.

00:38:05.875 --> 00:38:08.275
We're set for coaxial warp.

00:38:08.311 --> 00:38:09.835
Let's find Voyager.

00:38:16.119 --> 00:38:18.781
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:38:18.821 --> 00:38:21.415
The Doctor has treated
Mr. Paris' phaser wounds,

00:38:21.524 --> 00:38:24.084
but has been unable
to wake him.

00:38:24.127 --> 00:38:26.789
The motive for his attack
remains a mystery.

00:38:26.829 --> 00:38:29.093
Neurological scans
yielded very little,

00:38:29.132 --> 00:38:31.032
but l did find something
very interesting

00:38:31.067 --> 00:38:32.557
in his blood analysis.

00:38:34.137 --> 00:38:36.230
There are traces
of a second DNA pattern

00:38:36.272 --> 00:38:38.206
in his nucleotide structure.

00:38:38.241 --> 00:38:40.038
Possibly the result
of a genetic virus.

00:38:40.076 --> 00:38:42.772
Could this be the cause
of his recent behavior?

00:38:42.812 --> 00:38:45.144
L don't know,
but l'm running more scans

00:38:45.181 --> 00:38:46.546
to see how this
might have affected

00:38:46.583 --> 00:38:48.244
his neurological functions.

00:38:48.284 --> 00:38:51.151
Captain, a vessel just emerged

00:38:51.187 --> 00:38:53.621
from coaxial space
off our starboard bow.

00:38:53.656 --> 00:38:55.487
Keep me informed, Doctor.

00:39:05.568 --> 00:39:06.830
Hail them.

00:39:08.171 --> 00:39:09.798
Captain Janeway.

00:39:09.839 --> 00:39:13.673
Welcome back, Mr. Steth.

00:39:13.710 --> 00:39:15.234
L know this sounds crazy,
Captain,

00:39:15.278 --> 00:39:16.370
but l'm not Steth.

00:39:16.412 --> 00:39:18.073
L'm Tom Paris.

00:39:19.515 --> 00:39:21.415
L beg your pardon.

00:39:21.517 --> 00:39:23.348
We're dealing with an alien
who's some sort

00:39:23.386 --> 00:39:24.410
of identity thief.

00:39:24.454 --> 00:39:26.251
He traded places with me.

00:39:26.289 --> 00:39:29.258
Please beam us aboard.

00:39:30.860 --> 00:39:34.318
Maintain your position
while we consider your request.

00:39:34.364 --> 00:39:35.888
End transmission.

00:39:35.932 --> 00:39:38.264
Hold him in a tractor beam
until you hear from me.

00:39:38.301 --> 00:39:39.268
Aye, Captain.

00:39:39.302 --> 00:39:41.429
L have a feeling Steth
and his new friend

00:39:41.537 --> 00:39:42.868
are behind whatever's
happened to Tom.

00:39:42.905 --> 00:39:43.872
Captain?

00:39:43.906 --> 00:39:45.703
No time to explain.
L'll be in Sick Bay.

00:40:00.723 --> 00:40:02.247
Captain?

00:40:08.598 --> 00:40:11.226
Commander, l'm reading
an unauthorized shuttle launch.

00:40:12.935 --> 00:40:14.402
It's the Captain.

00:40:14.437 --> 00:40:16.268
She's in the shuttle
Tom's been working on.

00:40:16.306 --> 00:40:17.637
Try hailing her.

00:40:17.674 --> 00:40:20.006
She's not responding.

00:40:20.043 --> 00:40:21.442
Hail Steth's ship.

00:40:23.346 --> 00:40:25.576
Look, l don't know who you are,

00:40:25.615 --> 00:40:27.583
but l want to know
what's happening here.

00:40:27.617 --> 00:40:28.584
Who's on that shuttle?

00:40:28.618 --> 00:40:29.744
Captain Janeway.

00:40:29.786 --> 00:40:31.447
No. L'm betting the alien

00:40:31.487 --> 00:40:35.014
switched my body...
Tom's body for hers.

00:40:35.058 --> 00:40:36.855
You've got to let us out
of this tractor beam.

00:40:36.893 --> 00:40:38.155
We can catch her with this ship.

00:40:38.194 --> 00:40:40.458
Chakotay...

00:40:40.496 --> 00:40:41.463
it's me.

00:40:41.497 --> 00:40:42.828
How do l know that?

00:40:45.301 --> 00:40:47.098
The other day in your office,

00:40:47.136 --> 00:40:48.797
you told me
l'd turned my life around.

00:40:48.838 --> 00:40:51.602
Well, give me the chance
to prove it.

00:40:51.641 --> 00:40:53.108
Let me go after the shuttle.

00:40:53.142 --> 00:40:54.404
It is the only way

00:40:54.444 --> 00:40:56.605
we can get everybody
back into the right body.

00:40:57.647 --> 00:40:59.376
Harry...

00:40:59.415 --> 00:41:01.406
disengage the tractor beam.

00:41:08.157 --> 00:41:11.285
20,000 kilometers and closing.

00:41:11.327 --> 00:41:12.726
Has he detected us yet?

00:41:14.230 --> 00:41:16.323
L'd say he has.

00:41:19.402 --> 00:41:23.202
Gentlemen, l'd advise you
to reconsider this pursuit.

00:41:23.239 --> 00:41:26.470
Killing me will only keep you
trapped in those bodies.

00:41:26.576 --> 00:41:27.838
He's right.

00:41:27.877 --> 00:41:29.071
We can't risk killing him.

00:41:29.112 --> 00:41:31.876
Yeah, but nothing's keeping
him from killing us.

00:41:31.914 --> 00:41:35.281
Damn! The ship's not nearly
as maneuverable as a shuttle.

00:41:35.318 --> 00:41:36.410
Shields are down.

00:41:36.452 --> 00:41:38.215
L'm surprised you're so eager

00:41:38.254 --> 00:41:40.654
to reclaim your life
on Voyager, Tom.

00:41:40.690 --> 00:41:43.386
L was just as disappointed
with it as you were.

00:41:43.426 --> 00:41:45.724
Then l guess we were both wrong.

00:41:45.762 --> 00:41:48.026
It's time to move on again.

00:41:48.064 --> 00:41:52.194
Oh, Tom... be sure to send
my best regards to B'Elanna.

00:41:52.235 --> 00:41:53.395
Hmm?

00:41:55.371 --> 00:41:58.067
He's charging the coaxial drive.

00:41:58.107 --> 00:42:00.075
Set the sensors to track him.

00:42:00.109 --> 00:42:01.736
L can't. He's blocking us.

00:42:01.778 --> 00:42:07.148
We won't be able to follow him
once he goes into coaxial warp.

00:42:10.686 --> 00:42:11.880
We're losing him!

00:42:11.921 --> 00:42:13.912
The carburetor!

00:42:13.956 --> 00:42:16.186
We added a polaric modulator

00:42:16.225 --> 00:42:17.419
to the coaxial drive.

00:42:17.460 --> 00:42:20.156
If l can target the modulator,

00:42:20.196 --> 00:42:21.993
hit it
with a chromoelectric pulse,

00:42:22.031 --> 00:42:23.794
that'll disrupt his engines.

00:42:23.833 --> 00:42:26.028
Here goes.

00:42:34.944 --> 00:42:37.378
L hope you still have
my box wrench.

00:42:37.413 --> 00:42:40.177
Faulty carburetors
can be a pain to fix.

00:42:43.352 --> 00:42:47.311
Captain's Log, Stardate 51775.2.

00:42:47.356 --> 00:42:48.880
While the alien intruder

00:42:48.925 --> 00:42:51.621
remains trapped in the body
of his last victim,

00:42:51.661 --> 00:42:55.188
the Doctor has found a way
to return Tom, Steth and me

00:42:55.231 --> 00:42:56.926
to our own bodies.

00:42:56.966 --> 00:42:59.696
Doctor,
l can't thank you enough.

00:42:59.735 --> 00:43:01.862
You've given me my life back.

00:43:01.904 --> 00:43:03.667
All in a day's work.

00:43:03.706 --> 00:43:05.731
There were times when l thought

00:43:05.775 --> 00:43:07.606
l would be stuck
in that body forever.

00:43:07.643 --> 00:43:08.701
And believe me,

00:43:08.744 --> 00:43:11.178
l'm just as happy to be back
to the old Tom Paris.

00:43:11.214 --> 00:43:13.045
What do you plan to do now?

00:43:13.082 --> 00:43:15.107
L'm going to take
her back to Bentha.

00:43:15.151 --> 00:43:18.211
L hope to find the person
who belongs to that body.

00:43:18.254 --> 00:43:20.449
But who knows
if that's the end of it?

00:43:20.556 --> 00:43:23.423
We have no idea
how long she or he

00:43:23.459 --> 00:43:25.154
has been switching identities.

00:43:25.194 --> 00:43:27.162
It may take a while...

00:43:28.664 --> 00:43:30.825
but l will do whatever l can

00:43:30.867 --> 00:43:33.802
to find everyone
you've violated.

00:43:33.836 --> 00:43:36.566
A security team will
escort her to your ship

00:43:36.606 --> 00:43:39.507
and erect a force field
to contain her.

00:43:54.891 --> 00:43:57.189
So this is where
you've been hiding?

00:43:57.226 --> 00:43:58.818
A garage?

00:43:58.861 --> 00:44:02.262
Lt's more than just a garage.

00:44:02.298 --> 00:44:04.528
This is a monument

00:44:04.567 --> 00:44:07.092
to hundreds and hundreds
of hours...

00:44:07.136 --> 00:44:10.264
that l probably should
have spent with you.

00:44:10.306 --> 00:44:12.331
Probably?

00:44:12.375 --> 00:44:14.309
Definitely.

00:44:16.245 --> 00:44:19.214
It's a lovely garage, Tom,

00:44:19.248 --> 00:44:21.978
but l still don't understand
why you brought me here.

00:44:22.018 --> 00:44:26.455
Well, consider it
a symbolic gesture.

00:44:26.522 --> 00:44:31.983
It's my less-than-subtle attempt
to... let you in.

00:44:32.028 --> 00:44:33.791
L see.

00:44:33.829 --> 00:44:38.391
To make it clear that l mean
almost as much to you as a...

00:44:38.434 --> 00:44:40.231
a cam-a-ro.

00:44:40.269 --> 00:44:43.067
It's a mint condition

00:44:43.105 --> 00:44:45.073
1969...

00:44:46.742 --> 00:44:49.006
ca-mare-oh.

00:44:49.045 --> 00:44:52.014
And, yes... you mean
a lot more to me.
